5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:21:23-07:00","id":948063,"title":"","content":"Biting Aura (page 158) has no dicepool.<br /> Also, is Veritas (page 160) supposed to be equal to or <i>greater than</i> your Azoth? That means being a stronger more powerful Promethean makes your Alembic bonus weaker. But then, if it's supposed to read &quot;equal to or less than&quot;, then stronger powers would be harder to pick up than weaker ones. It really feels like it should be sensing powers regardless of your Azoth rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 08-10-2016, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:05:03-07:00","id":948154,"title":"","content":"Under Gaining Transmutations header, page 118, the book says<br /> <br /> &quot;When a Promethean adopts a new Refinement, the player selects one Alembic from each Transmutation. These are the only Alembics the promethean has access to upon first alignment. With each new Role mastered within a Refinement, the player may select another Alembic each Transmutation; upon mastering the third Role, the entire Transmutation is available&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of the text for the Transmutations give a distinct feeling that these were supposed to be taken in a bottom-up order, and not free-form, using wording like &quot;Building apon his knowledge of X&quot; as in &quot;building on the last transmutation, you now can do more powerful stuff&quot; and &quot;At this level of charge&quot; (which really means &quot;by expending 1 pyros&quot; but comes across as &quot;at this level of mastery&quot; as in Mage. I will edit this post as I re-read these and get specific examples.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> Ok, on another read, I kinda get this now. It was actually triggered by the different headers. The breakdown of the system as I understand it now is<br /> <br /> Transmutation<br /> Alembic 1<br /> Alembic 2<br /> Alembic 3<br /> Alembic 4<br /> <br /> And each alembic can be used with either 1, 2 or 3 pyros expenditure.<br /> <br /> I might just be me being stupid, but I think the structure of them could be explained a bit better and in a more direct, plain manner. Perhaps more of a distinction between the headers (different font between Alembic large bold and charge slightly smaller bold).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5761,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","user":"ShadowJakkal","date":". 08-10-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","name":"ShadowJakkal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:31:00-07:00","id":948189,"title":"","content":"On Pages 133, 134, 136 it references a &quot;Notoriety Condition&quot;<br /> <br /> but it is nowhere to be found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:30:59-07:00","id":948228,"title":"","content":"Page 176, it's minor, but the chart is messed up <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/7DrJN58.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#433471\"><span style=\"font-family:Fluoxetine\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Effects of a Wasteland</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">A Wasteland starts small and increases in size and potency over time. The size is tracked on the chart above, and the following five categories track the potency. Each category also imposes a penalty to all rolls to resist Torment within the threshold.<br /> Wastelands cause objects and people within to suffer weakness, frailty, and brittleness. Each category lists penalties to Health and Durability. Structure and Durability losses reflect on all objects in the area, and are imposed over the first day an object is within. Objects reduced to 0 Structure fall to worthlessness after that time. Health penalties act as bashing damage applied to humans within. They may not heal that damage while within the Wasteland. Note that this applies only to humans; Prometheans are immune to these Wasteland effects.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Should be \u20133 instead of -3 and the write up mentions humans (and presumably other animals) taking Bashing damage when inside of a Wasteland, but that's not listed in the chart.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 08-10-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:12:11-07:00","id":948455,"title":"","content":"P.256: The Scholar has &quot;PErfected Bezoars&quot; listed as her Dread Powers, but it is not described anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:53:25-07:00","id":948520,"title":"","content":"Several references to the Informed Condition throughout the book, but it's missing from the appendix. One can sub in the Condition from another ChroD book, but it should probably be included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:20:27-07:00","id":948555,"title":"","content":"<b>pg. 124</b> &quot;For every point of pyros spent charging <b>this level of</b> the Alembic&quot;. The rules at the beginning of the section say that you pour pyros into the alembic, unlocking more advanced distillations, rather than charging individual distillations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:41:56-07:00","id":948649,"title":"","content":"<b>p4, cross-ref. pp144-150:</b> Mesmerism and Metamorphosis sections are out of order in what is otherwise an alphabetized Transmutation list.<br /> <br /> <b>p88:</b> &quot;In that instant, Vitriol surges inside him, and he finally understands what it is to be a Muse. He achieves the Role's milestone and can now move on.&quot; There is no &quot;Muse&quot; Role in any of the Refinements; although the character in question is a Galateid, his Lineage is not the milestone-providing element under discussion in this section. Possibly the Aurum Role &quot;Companion&quot; is applicable instead?<br /> <br /> <b>p63, cross-ref. pp125-8 and pp147-50:</b> &quot;Seeing weakness in others is precisely so that he can identify it in himself. It eventually gives him a measure of control over his own Torment that no other Promethean can achieve.&quot; Though Quell Torment was a Contamination Transmutation in 1e, there is no similar effect in either Contamination or Mesmerism in 2e and the nearest similar power (using Catharsis to relieve your own Tormented Condition) provides no explicit self-targeting workaround for the power's requirement of eye-contact.<br /> <br /> <b>p128, cross-ref. pp308-9:</b> Onset of Madness seems to lack a meaningful mechanical effect; all of the effects of the Disquieted Condition except for Stage Four's complete lockout of social rolls apply to a specific Promethean. If the Condition is supposed to instead settle into referencing another target, this should probably be made explicit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:26:13-07:00","id":948847,"title":"","content":"All on page 110:<br /> <br /> &quot;With this Bestowment, your character acts without distraction or impairment in the same way that a ghost flows unnoticed through Twilight.&quot; Through Twilight implies it is a medium through which ghosts travel, rather than the form ghosts take. Should probably be in Twilight or as Twilight.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your character\u2019s flesh is attuned with the Twilight.&quot; The implies Twilight is a place. Should just be attuned with Twilight.<br /> <br /> &quot;Items she holds or wears cannot interact with entities in the Twilight.&quot; Again, should be entities in Twilight or Twilight entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:22:23-07:00","id":948898,"title":"","content":"A 10-Refinement New Dawn allows a Promethean to become human but retain one calcified Alembic. Some Alembics reference the character's Azoth rating, which a human would not have. Some clarification on what trait, if any, Redeemed should use in place of Azoth would be much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:12:03-07:00","id":948948,"title":"","content":"Page 113: &quot;A Companion is generally a being in the Twilight. Some Companions can manifest into the physical world, though.&quot;<br /> In addition to having the confusing &quot;the twilight&quot; phrasing, this whole sentence is extremely misleading because Twilight Form <i>is</i> a Manifestation, and it is used by ephemeral entities while they are in the physical world. Consider rephrasing, perhaps, &quot;A Companion generally exists in Twilight Form. Some Companions can manifest in other ways, though.&quot; or something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:24:35-07:00","id":948955,"title":"","content":"Not technically errata, but the Driven Merit is an absolute Beat machine. Might be a good idea to specify that Conditions granted by Driven don't grant Beats, or at least that only negative Conditions do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:27:25-07:00","id":948956,"title":"","content":"The Famous Face Merit should probably have Promethean as a Prerequisite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T00:03:27-07:00","id":949163,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 124</b>, The Fortified Compact, 4th bullet: &quot;Humanity&quot; is mentioned instead of Pilgrimage.<br /> <b>p. 125</b>, Communal Font: &quot;The Sentry may forces&quot; should be &quot;The Sentry forces&quot;<br /> Also on p.125, What's Mine is Yours: &quot;Is&quot; should be capitalized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":".  added two more 08-12-2016, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T03:56:10-07:00","id":949223,"title":"","content":"Forcing Doors and Hard Leverage don't show up in the Social Maneuvering section on pages 202 to 204, even though they're both mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:48:21-07:00","id":949284,"title":"","content":"Page 40: &quot;Sharing a humor with another kind of Promethean doesn\u2019t make the Extempore just like a member of that Lineage, of course. (...) an Extempore tied to ectoplasm might be more closely died to the ghosts of the dead than the spirits of the natural world, with an accompanying difference in character.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 110: &quot;Whereas Osirans tease at the line between the living and the dead, Ulgan revel in the macabre. They\u2019re death warmed over and maintain strong ties to the Underworld. Ghosts, the hungry dead, shades: these are all kin to the Ulgan.&quot;<br /> <br /> These passages seem to contradict each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:13:50-07:00","id":949322,"title":"","content":"There is no listing for what Redeemed with Alembics use to substitute for Azoth when activating them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"re